That's beautiful. What is it?

13
00:02:15,970 --> 00:02:18,205
Sarah's favorite.

14
00:02:18,205 --> 00:02:20,240
She'd climb up
on the dining room table

15
00:02:20,307 --> 00:02:23,443
and sing that hymn
every time we had guests.

16
00:02:23,511 --> 00:02:25,513
Oh.

17
00:02:30,084 --> 00:02:31,119
Here you are.

18
00:02:31,218 --> 00:02:33,220
Oh, thank you.

19
00:02:34,088 --> 00:02:35,123
Julia.

20
00:02:35,222 --> 00:02:36,524
Right.

21
00:02:37,892 --> 00:02:39,927
Um, are those my keys?

22
00:02:39,994 --> 00:02:41,361
No.

23
00:02:41,428 --> 00:02:43,031
Evelyn.
I keep mace on there.

24
00:02:43,097 --> 00:02:44,464
They're mine.
No.

25
00:02:44,532 --> 00:02:47,769
I wouldn't want you
hurting yourself.

26
00:02:47,835 --> 00:02:49,302
What?

27
00:02:50,237 --> 00:02:51,973
Evelyn, please.

28
00:02:54,142 --> 00:02:56,744
Thank you.

29
00:02:56,811 --> 00:02:58,846
Why do you carry mace?

30
00:02:58,913 --> 00:03:01,348
Um, I live alone, so.

31
00:03:01,415 --> 00:03:03,718
But you live with me now.

32
00:03:07,121 --> 00:03:09,389
It's getting late.
We should get you to bed soon.

33
00:03:09,456 --> 00:03:12,827
I'll just check your
blood pressure first, okay?

34
00:03:17,765 --> 00:03:19,801
Okay.

35
00:03:26,574 --> 00:03:29,077
I want you
to put your hand right here.

36
00:03:29,143 --> 00:03:30,310
Hm.

37
00:03:30,377 --> 00:03:31,946
Is that comfortable?

38
00:03:36,050 --> 00:03:39,352
So, is Sarah your daughter?

39
00:03:41,856 --> 00:03:45,126
You know, we never locked
our doors when we were young.

40
00:03:46,194 --> 00:03:47,394
We had no need to.

41
00:03:47,461 --> 00:03:49,197
That must've been nice.

42
00:03:49,296 --> 00:03:51,398
It was nice.

43
00:03:51,465 --> 00:03:53,901
We'd be out all day,
wandering.

44
00:03:53,968 --> 00:03:57,805
Come home in the evening
and our parents never worried.

45
00:03:57,872 --> 00:04:01,743
Maybe they did.
Maybe you just didn't notice.

46
00:04:01,809 --> 00:04:03,044
Maybe.

47
00:04:16,023 --> 00:04:17,925
Okay.

48
00:04:17,992 --> 00:04:19,060
Am I okay?

49
00:04:19,127 --> 00:04:22,230
Yeah. 116 over 75.

50
00:04:22,329 --> 00:04:23,231
You're good.

51
00:04:23,330 --> 00:04:24,699
Hmm.

52
00:04:26,501 --> 00:04:28,503
Just hold on.

53
00:04:33,207 --> 00:04:35,643
Okay.

54
00:04:45,418 --> 00:04:46,854
Good.

55
00:04:48,421 --> 00:04:50,357
There's a storm coming.

56
00:04:50,423 --> 00:04:51,659
Yeah.

57
00:04:54,762 --> 00:04:57,364
I was supposed
to fix your room.

58
00:04:57,430 --> 00:04:59,767
Oh, it's fine.
My room was made up.

59
00:04:59,834 --> 00:05:01,035
Thank you.

60
00:05:06,574 --> 00:05:08,375
Are you done?

61
00:05:08,375 --> 00:05:09,844
Yes.

62
00:05:14,148 --> 00:05:15,983
Okay. That smells nice.

63
00:05:16,050 --> 00:05:17,285
Mm-hmm.

64
00:05:17,384 --> 00:05:20,288
Did we uh,
did I show you around?

65
00:05:20,387 --> 00:05:22,489
I have everything I need.
Thank you.

66
00:05:22,557 --> 00:05:24,959
All right. Hmm.

67
00:05:26,459 --> 00:05:29,664
I forget sometimes.

68
00:05:44,579 --> 00:05:46,714
How are you feeling?

69
00:05:46,781 --> 00:05:48,481
Like hell.

70
00:05:50,518 --> 00:05:52,419
Well, I'll be right
in the next room

71
00:05:52,452 --> 00:05:54,088
if you need anything.

72
00:05:54,822 --> 00:05:57,158
Thank you. Uh...

73
00:05:57,225 --> 00:05:58,726
Julia.

74
00:05:58,793 --> 00:06:02,530
Yes, Julia,
and I'm so sorry.

75
00:06:02,597 --> 00:06:05,432
No. No apologies.
It's fine.

76
00:06:07,501 --> 00:06:09,237
Goodnight.

77
00:06:09,303 --> 00:06:11,438
Goodnight, Sarah.

78
00:06:26,020 --> 00:06:29,857
Now I lay me down to sleep.

79
00:06:29,924 --> 00:06:33,861
I pray for all
the souls I keep.

80
00:06:35,763 --> 00:06:37,665
Shit!

81
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:29,016
Uh, shit.

82
00:07:35,523 --> 00:07:37,124
Hi, Dad.

83
00:07:38,893 --> 00:07:41,896
No, I'm not ignoring you.
I'm working.

84
00:07:43,531 --> 00:07:45,533
No, Dad,
I told you I probably--

85
00:07:45,599 --> 00:07:46,634
I'm not gonna make it.

86
00:07:49,804 --> 00:07:52,039
I'm not avoiding it.

87
00:07:55,643 --> 00:07:58,746
It's just,
I-- I just got this job.

88
00:07:58,813 --> 00:08:00,948
I can't leave a few days in.

89
00:08:06,654 --> 00:08:08,556
I don't know.

90
00:08:09,924 --> 00:08:11,859
I can't believe
you're asking this.

91
00:08:15,629 --> 00:08:17,765
Dad, I don't know.

92
00:08:19,567 --> 00:08:21,769
Ew.
No, never mind.

93
00:08:21,836 --> 00:08:23,270
I said I don't know,
because it's not

94
00:08:23,337 --> 00:08:24,605
that kind of job.

95
00:08:24,672 --> 00:08:27,375
It could be a few days,
a few weeks.

96
00:08:30,344 --> 00:08:33,881
Of course, I miss her.
What kind of question is that?

97
00:08:35,850 --> 00:08:37,284
Yeah, I get it, but...

98
00:08:40,454 --> 00:08:41,689
Well, what does it matter?

99
00:08:41,756 --> 00:08:44,392
No one's seen me there
in years.

100
00:08:46,894 --> 00:08:49,997
Uh, Dad, come on.
I don't go anymore.

101
00:08:50,064 --> 00:08:51,298
You know that.

102
00:08:56,971 --> 00:08:59,106
Well, what difference
does it make?

103
00:08:59,173 --> 00:09:02,610
It doesn't change anything.
Mom knew I loved her!

104
00:09:04,612 --> 00:09:07,248
Dad? Dad?

105
00:09:07,982 --> 00:09:11,218
Listen, I need to go,
so I'll call you again tomorrow

106
00:09:11,285 --> 00:09:13,254
and we can talk
about this then, okay?

107
00:09:15,122 --> 00:09:16,323
Yes, I promise.

108
00:09:18,626 --> 00:09:20,628
Okay.
I love you, too.

109
00:09:20,694 --> 00:09:22,696
Okay, bye.

110
00:09:49,023 --> 00:09:50,658
Jesus.

111
00:09:51,425 --> 00:09:56,931
Like, what is not clear about,
I'll call you to--

112
00:09:58,432 --> 00:10:01,268
What are you doing
in my house?

113
00:10:03,671 --> 00:10:05,239
Evelyn?

114
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:08,309
How do you know my name?

115
00:10:09,076 --> 00:10:14,583
I'm your nurse.
I just helped you to bed.

116
00:10:14,648 --> 00:10:17,151
We spoke about Sarah,
your daughter.

117
00:10:18,919 --> 00:10:21,188
How about you
give me that, yeah?

118
00:10:23,858 --> 00:10:26,561
Let's put it back
by the fireplace.

119
00:10:26,627 --> 00:10:31,232
What do you think?
Yeah? Please.

120
00:10:34,935 --> 00:10:37,071
Did you paint that?

121
00:10:39,140 --> 00:10:40,474
Yes.

122
00:10:41,075 --> 00:10:45,679
Very talented.
I'm quite terrible.

123
00:10:45,746 --> 00:10:47,281
You're an artist?

124
00:10:47,348 --> 00:10:48,883
Nothing serious.

125
00:10:52,554 --> 00:10:54,355
Are those yours, too?

126
00:10:56,657 --> 00:10:58,125
Mm-hmm.

127
00:10:58,192 --> 00:11:00,194
I'd love to see
your other paintings.

128
00:11:00,261 --> 00:11:02,796
-You can hold onto that
if it makes you feel better.
-Mm-hmm.

129
00:11:02,863 --> 00:11:04,365
Is that okay?

130
00:11:07,067 --> 00:11:08,002
Okay.

131
00:11:08,068 --> 00:11:09,103
Okay.

132
00:11:10,471 --> 00:11:11,540
Go first.

133
00:11:11,606 --> 00:11:13,440
Right. Yeah, sure.

134
00:11:13,508 --> 00:11:14,875
Okay.

135
00:11:20,414 --> 00:11:21,982
Wow.

136
00:11:23,817 --> 00:11:25,953
I love the-- the detail
on this one.

137
00:11:26,020 --> 00:11:26,887
Mm.

138
00:11:26,954 --> 00:11:28,155
You have a real eye for color.

139
00:11:28,222 --> 00:11:30,157
The way they
contrast each other.

140
00:11:30,224 --> 00:11:33,093
I would've never guessed
these go together, but they do.

141
00:11:35,095 --> 00:11:38,032
My mom taught me everything.

142
00:11:38,098 --> 00:11:40,334
She had an eye like you do.

143
00:11:41,936 --> 00:11:43,804
Is this you?

144
00:11:44,639 --> 00:11:46,774
Long time ago.

145
00:11:47,642 --> 00:11:49,443
And that's your family?

146
00:11:49,511 --> 00:11:50,545
Yeah.

147
00:11:50,612 --> 00:11:52,012
Hmm.

148
00:11:53,347 --> 00:11:55,249
Anthropology.

149
00:11:55,316 --> 00:11:57,351
That's the study
of culture, right?

150
00:11:57,418 --> 00:12:00,821
Art and rituals,
and things like that?

151
00:12:02,189 --> 00:12:05,826
Oh, Randall gave me that
for our first anniversary.

152
00:12:05,893 --> 00:12:08,462
He got it at a, uh,
an art supply store

153
00:12:08,530 --> 00:12:12,866
and then he buried it
at our picnic spot.

154
00:12:12,933 --> 00:12:15,436
Is Randall the guy in the photo?

155
00:12:17,471 --> 00:12:21,408
Yeah. He-- he painted, too,

156
00:12:21,475 --> 00:12:24,512
but he took this photograph

157
00:12:24,579 --> 00:12:27,881
of me just before our wedding.

158
00:12:27,948 --> 00:12:30,084
That's the biggest smile
I've ever seen.

159
00:12:30,150 --> 00:12:31,452
Yeah.

160
00:12:32,186 --> 00:12:34,288
He must've been very special.

161
00:12:35,956 --> 00:12:38,058
We were happy.

162
00:12:39,960 --> 00:12:41,395
Hey, it's getting late.

163
00:12:41,462 --> 00:12:44,465
How about we get back,
we get you back to bed?

164
00:12:47,502 --> 00:12:49,837
I'll put this back.

165
00:13:01,583 --> 00:13:02,517
I'm sorry.

166
00:13:02,584 --> 00:13:04,719
No, it's fine.

167
00:13:04,852 --> 00:13:06,320
Julia?

168
00:13:06,387 --> 00:13:07,522
Yeah.

169
00:13:19,601 --> 00:13:21,201
You okay?

170
00:13:26,641 --> 00:13:28,309
Watch your step.

171
00:13:34,415 --> 00:13:36,116
Here we are.

172
00:13:42,923 --> 00:13:45,025
There you go.

173
00:13:45,459 --> 00:13:46,761
Oh.

174
00:13:48,329 --> 00:13:50,064
Thank you, Julia.

175
00:13:51,899 --> 00:13:54,168
What happened to your hands?

176
00:13:54,234 --> 00:13:55,903
Oh.

177
00:13:55,969 --> 00:13:57,672
Oh, nothing.

178
00:13:57,739 --> 00:13:59,607
Just old scars.

179
00:13:59,674 --> 00:14:00,908
Hmm.

180
00:14:04,646 --> 00:14:06,980
That is one gorgeous necklace.

181
00:14:07,047 --> 00:14:10,518
Oh, why thank you.
It was my mother's.

182
00:14:10,585 --> 00:14:12,052
Is that gold?

183
00:14:12,119 --> 00:14:15,022
Um, I think so, yeah.

184
00:14:15,089 --> 00:14:17,391
What a lovely piece.

185
00:14:19,927 --> 00:14:22,129
Oh, my.

186
00:14:22,196 --> 00:14:24,298
Do you think
you could help me down?

187
00:14:24,365 --> 00:14:25,432
Of course.

188
00:14:28,302 --> 00:14:30,805
That's it. There we go.

189
00:14:30,938 --> 00:14:32,439
Oh, my.

190
00:14:35,309 --> 00:14:38,946
Ooh, you know,
all my bones creak.

191
00:14:42,517 --> 00:14:43,450
Okay.

192
00:14:43,518 --> 00:14:44,552
Ooh.

193
00:14:45,754 --> 00:14:48,188
Hmm, pray with me.

194
00:14:48,255 --> 00:14:49,490
Pardon?

195
00:14:51,526 --> 00:14:53,427
Pray with me.

196
00:14:55,563 --> 00:15:00,167
I used to think that
prayer was ridiculous, too,

197
00:15:00,234 --> 00:15:04,873
before Sarah,
but somehow asking

198
00:15:04,972 --> 00:15:09,376
