for something seems arrogant.

199
00:15:09,443 --> 00:15:10,879
Hmm.

200
00:15:10,978 --> 00:15:14,883
But there is grace
in supplication.

201
00:15:14,982 --> 00:15:16,417
Hmm?

202
00:15:16,483 --> 00:15:19,987
I don't really pray
to God anymore.

203
00:15:20,855 --> 00:15:23,490
Who said anything about God?

204
00:15:26,561 --> 00:15:30,698
Thank you, dear.
Now clasp your hands.

205
00:15:36,303 --> 00:15:41,709
Now I lay me down to sleep.

206
00:15:41,776 --> 00:15:43,310
Go on.

207
00:15:43,778 --> 00:15:45,713
Now I lay me down to sleep.

208
00:15:47,214 --> 00:15:52,587
I pray for all the souls I keep.

209
00:15:52,654 --> 00:15:57,659
If I should die
before I wake,

210
00:15:57,725 --> 00:16:02,429
I pray the souls
another body will take.

211
00:16:04,331 --> 00:16:08,770
If I should live
for a few more days,

212
00:16:08,837 --> 00:16:14,074
I pray my keeper
to guide my ways.

213
00:16:14,141 --> 00:16:16,443
In my name,

214
00:16:16,511 --> 00:16:18,078
I pray,

215
00:16:18,145 --> 00:16:20,548
I pray,

216
00:16:20,615 --> 00:16:23,050
I pray.

217
00:16:24,819 --> 00:16:29,256
Now I lay me down to sleep.

218
00:16:29,323 --> 00:16:34,261
I pray for all
of the souls I keep.

219
00:16:34,328 --> 00:16:38,198
If I should die
before I wake,

220
00:16:38,265 --> 00:16:43,605
I pray the souls
another body will take.

221
00:16:43,671 --> 00:16:47,374
If I should live
for a few more days,

222
00:16:47,441 --> 00:16:51,779
I pray my keeper
to guide my way.

223
00:16:51,846 --> 00:16:53,447
Okay.

224
00:17:29,116 --> 00:17:33,521
Yeah.
Uh, yeah, I'll just...

225
00:17:35,122 --> 00:17:36,724
Later.

226
00:18:44,191 --> 00:18:45,459
Not bad.

227
00:18:51,666 --> 00:18:53,266
That's cute.

228
00:18:56,070 --> 00:18:57,572
That's gross.

229
00:19:05,079 --> 00:19:08,049
Color contrast, my ass.

230
00:19:08,116 --> 00:19:09,617
You're one dark lady.

231
00:19:13,888 --> 00:19:15,890
Yeah, you're okay.

232
00:19:50,257 --> 00:19:52,259
Weird.

233
00:23:27,742 --> 00:23:32,479
Evelyn? Are you up again?

234
00:24:00,374 --> 00:24:01,575
Can I help you?

235
00:24:01,642 --> 00:24:03,044
Is Evelyn home?

236
00:24:03,110 --> 00:24:04,345
Sorry, who are you?

237
00:24:04,412 --> 00:24:07,415
Randall.
You're Julia, right?

238
00:24:07,515 --> 00:24:09,850
Your agency put us in touch.

239
00:24:09,917 --> 00:24:12,153
Yeah, yeah.
Of course, hi.

240
00:24:12,219 --> 00:24:13,421
Come in.

241
00:24:19,060 --> 00:24:19,927
You're Evelyn's husband.

242
00:24:19,994 --> 00:24:23,331
Well, not for a long time now.

243
00:24:23,397 --> 00:24:24,832
Oh.

244
00:24:24,899 --> 00:24:26,233
Is she up?

245
00:24:26,300 --> 00:24:27,768
I just put her to bed.

246
00:24:27,835 --> 00:24:31,238
I hope she's awake.
I drove a long way out.

247
00:24:31,305 --> 00:24:34,342
She should be.
She was just praying, so...

248
00:24:34,408 --> 00:24:36,110
Evie, praying?

249
00:24:37,345 --> 00:24:38,813
Yeah.

250
00:24:51,258 --> 00:24:53,861
Did you-- did you hit the storm
on the way here?

251
00:24:53,928 --> 00:24:56,364
No, I came
from the other direction.

252
00:24:56,998 --> 00:24:59,667
I hope it doesn't get too bad.

253
00:24:59,734 --> 00:25:02,570
How is she doing?

254
00:25:02,603 --> 00:25:04,839
Uh, it's been
a pretty rough night.

255
00:25:04,905 --> 00:25:07,875
She's been kind of in and out.

256
00:25:09,677 --> 00:25:11,779
She spoke about you, though.

257
00:25:16,117 --> 00:25:17,818
Is something wrong?

258
00:25:19,086 --> 00:25:20,321
No.

259
00:25:21,222 --> 00:25:26,160
Uh, no. It's just,
I haven't seen this one
in a long time.

260
00:26:26,353 --> 00:26:28,656
There she is.

261
00:26:28,656 --> 00:26:30,224
Randall?

262
00:26:30,291 --> 00:26:31,292
Hey, Evie.

263
00:26:31,358 --> 00:26:32,760
Huh.

264
00:26:35,162 --> 00:26:36,664
You got old.

265
00:26:36,664 --> 00:26:38,899
Yeah, they say that happens.

266
00:26:39,967 --> 00:26:42,369
You're still as lovely as ever.

267
00:26:43,070 --> 00:26:45,106
And you're still full of shit.

268
00:26:46,774 --> 00:26:48,042
I've missed you.

269
00:26:48,109 --> 00:26:49,310
I know.

270
00:26:52,379 --> 00:26:54,448
Is Earl here with you?

271
00:26:54,516 --> 00:26:59,186
My brother died 12 years ago.
You went to the funeral.

272
00:27:00,754 --> 00:27:02,156
I did?

273
00:27:02,223 --> 00:27:03,924
It's okay.

274
00:27:03,991 --> 00:27:06,694
None of us are
what we used to be, right?

275
00:27:09,730 --> 00:27:11,699
And Marlene?

276
00:27:11,699 --> 00:27:12,967
She left me.

277
00:27:13,033 --> 00:27:15,236
That's been
a long time now, too.

278
00:27:16,237 --> 00:27:17,171
I'm sorry.

279
00:27:18,239 --> 00:27:20,141
No, you're not.

280
00:27:20,207 --> 00:27:21,375
No, I'm not.

281
00:27:24,546 --> 00:27:26,280
How long are you staying?

282
00:27:26,347 --> 00:27:27,748
As long as I need to.

283
00:27:28,916 --> 00:27:31,218
You have help now,

284
00:27:31,285 --> 00:27:34,255
so you don't need to worry
about anything.

285
00:27:35,923 --> 00:27:38,325
You have been thinking
about her.

286
00:27:38,859 --> 00:27:40,728
Every day.

287
00:27:41,729 --> 00:27:43,330
Me too.

288
00:27:48,335 --> 00:27:50,771
So why are you here?

289
00:27:57,778 --> 00:28:00,381
Where did you find
this inscription?

290
00:28:01,916 --> 00:28:04,418
Why didn't you wait
for me to get back?

291
00:28:04,485 --> 00:28:08,956
We could've discussed it,
figured out something together.

292
00:28:10,357 --> 00:28:14,495
Where is it, Evelyn?
I know you have it.

293
00:28:14,563 --> 00:28:15,796
No.

294
00:28:15,863 --> 00:28:17,097
Nobody else knows
where we buried it.

295
00:28:17,164 --> 00:28:19,534
No. No.

296
00:28:19,601 --> 00:28:21,769
-Why would you take it?
-No.

297
00:28:21,835 --> 00:28:25,674
If it's for this,
you know what can happen.

298
00:28:26,273 --> 00:28:28,209
- Where is it?
- Hey.

299
00:28:28,275 --> 00:28:29,076
Go away.

300
00:28:29,143 --> 00:28:30,244
I'm trying to protect you!

301
00:28:30,311 --> 00:28:32,846
-No.
-Hey! Don't touch her.

302
00:28:32,913 --> 00:28:36,217
Leave me, leave me,
leave me alone.

303
00:28:37,918 --> 00:28:39,554
Go away.

304
00:28:39,621 --> 00:28:42,524
You need to leave.
Now.

305
00:28:48,095 --> 00:28:49,664
Make him go. Make him go.

306
00:28:49,797 --> 00:28:50,864
Okay.

307
00:28:50,931 --> 00:28:51,932
Make sure he leaves.

308
00:28:51,999 --> 00:28:53,367
I promise.

309
00:28:54,034 --> 00:28:56,036
I don't wanna see him.

310
00:28:56,103 --> 00:28:58,339
If you don't get out
of this house in 30 seconds,

311
00:28:58,405 --> 00:29:01,308
I'm calling the police.
I don't care who you are.

312
00:29:04,345 --> 00:29:07,348
You have no idea
what's going on here.

313
00:29:13,087 --> 00:29:14,154
Yeah.

314
00:29:14,221 --> 00:29:15,489
It's gonna be okay, all right?

315
00:29:15,557 --> 00:29:18,492
Please, please get rid of him.

316
00:29:18,560 --> 00:29:20,294
I never wanna see him again.

317
00:29:20,361 --> 00:29:22,564
All right, just--
just calm down.

318
00:29:22,631 --> 00:29:24,164
I'll be right back.

319
00:29:28,035 --> 00:29:30,070
Where are you hiding it?

320
00:29:30,137 --> 00:29:32,873
Hey! Get out!

321
00:29:53,394 --> 00:29:55,296
Just leave!

322
00:29:57,064 --> 00:29:59,867
Watch yourself.

323
00:30:45,412 --> 00:30:48,916
Evelyn, what are you doing?
It's freezing.

324
00:30:51,018 --> 00:30:53,588
I wanna be out here
when I pass.

325
00:30:54,556 --> 00:30:57,324
Let's not talk about
that. You've still got time.

326
00:30:59,259 --> 00:31:02,229
Why would anyone
want a job like this?

327
00:31:03,230 --> 00:31:06,367
Why would you want to
watch someone die?

328
00:31:07,669 --> 00:31:10,270
Because no one
should have to die alone.

329
00:31:11,840 --> 00:31:14,041
We all die alone.

330
00:31:14,942 --> 00:31:16,678
What was that all
about up there?

331
00:31:17,545 --> 00:31:21,783
Oh, we don't agree on things.
 We never did, really.

332
00:31:22,751 --> 00:31:26,954
I tried to get him
to understand
but he-- he blames me.

333
00:31:28,389 --> 00:31:30,257
What happened to Sarah?

334
00:31:32,159 --> 00:31:36,263
Oh, Sarah.
I miss her so much.

335
00:31:39,099 --> 00:31:40,702
Can't hide from our past.

336
00:31:40,769 --> 00:31:44,506
Sometimes we have
to confront it and accept it.

337
00:31:46,708 --> 00:31:47,809
Is everything okay?

338
00:31:47,876 --> 00:31:49,977
I'm going to be sick.

339
00:31:49,977 --> 00:31:52,547
Come on,
let's go inside.

340
00:31:58,118 --> 00:32:00,622
Oh, dear. Come here.

341
00:32:03,792 --> 00:32:05,727
Ugh, oh, I'm so sorry.

342
00:32:05,794 --> 00:32:07,829
No, it's okay. It's fine.

343
00:32:07,896 --> 00:32:11,165
Let's get you cleaned up, okay?
I'll find you a blanket.

344
00:32:26,146 --> 00:32:27,381
All right.

345
00:32:33,755 --> 00:32:35,723
Evelyn?

346
00:32:43,531 --> 00:32:46,200
Oh, my... Evelyn?

347
00:32:47,735 --> 00:32:49,604
Evelyn, what are you doing?

348
00:32:51,271 --> 00:32:52,507
Stop that, please.

349
00:33:01,148 --> 00:33:02,349
Evelyn!

350
00:33:07,956 --> 00:33:09,557
Stop.

351
00:33:15,964 --> 00:33:17,297
Eve--

352
00:33:26,608 --> 00:33:28,743
Jesus Christ.

353
00:33:29,376 --> 00:33:31,245
<i>It's not working.</i>

354
00:33:31,311 --> 00:33:34,649
<i>The song will work.</i>
<i>It always works.</i>

355
00:33:34,716 --> 00:33:35,917
<i>Brush my hair.</i>

356
00:33:35,984 --> 00:33:37,284
<i>What the fuck is this?</i>

357
00:33:37,351 --> 00:33:39,119
<i>Sure, my love.</i>

358
00:33:40,922 --> 00:33:44,091
<i>It don't feel so good.</i>
<i>My tummy hurts.</i>

359
00:33:45,092 --> 00:33:47,327
<i>Do you want me</i>
<i>to rub your tummy?</i>

360
00:33:49,329 --> 00:33:50,598
<i>Mom?</i>

361
00:33:50,665 --> 00:33:52,332
<i>What is it?</i>

362
00:33:52,399 --> 00:33:54,368
<i>Why do you have that?</i>

363
00:33:54,434 --> 00:33:56,236
<i>Oh, this?</i>

364
00:33:56,303 --> 00:33:58,540
<i>Are you taping me?</i>

365
00:33:58,606 --> 00:34:01,275
- <i>I...</i>
- Where the fuck am I?

366
00:34:01,341 --> 00:34:03,778
<i>I was-- I was worried about you</i>
<i>and wanted to record</i>

367
00:34:03,845 --> 00:34:05,145
<i>any changes.</i>

368
00:34:05,212 --> 00:34:07,281
<i>Changes?</i>

369
00:34:07,347 --> 00:34:10,484
<i>Sorry, I should've asked you.</i>
<i>I'll turn it off.</i>

370
00:34:12,119 --> 00:34:13,555
<i>Is it off?</i>

371
00:34:13,621 --> 00:34:15,222
<i>Yes.</i>

372
00:34:16,758 --> 00:34:18,292
<i>Don't ever do that again!</i>

373
00:34:18,358 --> 00:34:19,994
shit.

374
00:34:20,127 --> 00:34:21,261
<i>Sarah?</i>

375
00:34:21,328 --> 00:34:23,163
<i>Get out!</i>

376
00:34:25,332 --> 00:34:27,134
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

377
00:34:44,184 --> 00:34:45,720
Okay.

378
00:34:54,261 --> 00:34:56,798
Oh, my God, Evelyn,
what did you do?

379
00:35:14,181 --> 00:35:15,917
What the hell?

380
00:35:30,798 --> 00:35:32,232
What is this?

381
00:36:36,664 --> 00:36:38,265
Hello?

382
00:37:02,456 --> 00:37:05,292
What... What is...

383
00:37:14,001 --> 00:37:15,837
What the fuck?

384
00:37:27,749 --> 00:37:30,317
Is there a back door?

385
00:37:30,317 --> 00:37:32,419
I think I can open it.

386
00:37:33,320 --> 00:37:35,223
Pete!

387
00:37:35,322 --> 00:37:36,791
Go check upstairs.

388
00:37:36,858 --> 00:37:38,726
Sh-- shit.

389
00:37:39,927 --> 00:37:40,862
Oh!

390
00:38:11,058 --> 00:38:13,060
Office is clear.

391
00:38:16,197 --> 00:38:18,365
Kitchen's clear.

392
00:38:19,967 --> 00:38:22,904
Evelyn, where are you?
I just want to talk!

393
00:38:42,389 --> 00:38:43,891
Okay.

394
00:39:35,843 --> 00:39:36,777
Hey.

395
00:39:37,645 --> 00:39:40,781
Oh, fuck! Oh!

396
00:39:44,886 --> 00:39:45,987
Calm down.

397
00:39:46,053 --> 00:39:48,556
Where do I go?
Where the fuck do I go?

398
00:39:50,258 --> 00:39:51,692
Shit!

399
00:39:55,963 --> 00:39:58,532
Okay, okay.

400
00:39:58,599 --> 00:40:00,034
Just find something.

401
00:40:00,101 --> 00:40:01,602
There's gotta be something
in here.

402
00:40:01,669 --> 00:40:04,972
Okay. Find scissors.

403
00:40:06,173 --> 00:40:07,208
Okay.

404
00:40:07,275 --> 00:40:09,577
Shit.
Fucking...

405
00:40:11,279 --> 00:40:13,581
Fucking shit!

406
00:40:15,016 --> 00:40:16,350
She blinded me, man.

407
00:40:16,416 --> 00:40:17,718
Yeah, well.

408
00:40:17,785 --> 00:40:18,819
- I'm scared.
- Quiet!

409
00:40:18,886 --> 00:40:20,420
It fucking burns!

410
00:40:20,487 --> 00:40:22,489
Hey, man up!
You grab him.

411
00:40:22,556 --> 00:40:24,025
I can't look
for anyone right now.

412
00:40:24,091 --> 00:40:25,026
Hey, shut up. All right?

413
00:40:25,092 --> 00:40:27,228
Just be quiet.

414
00:40:27,295 --> 00:40:28,729
We just want to talk.

415
00:40:28,796 --> 00:40:30,430
We're running out of time.

416
00:40:30,497 --> 00:40:32,934
Give me a minute.
Go downstairs.

417
00:40:34,501 --> 00:40:37,371
I'm not gonna hurt anybody.
Can we talk?

418
00:40:37,437 --> 00:40:38,572
I'd like to explain.

419
00:40:38,639 --> 00:40:39,941
Stay away!

420
00:40:40,007 --> 00:40:41,742
This is not how
I wanted this to go.

421
00:40:41,809 --> 00:40:44,178
How did you
want this to go?

422
00:40:44,245 --> 00:40:45,746
This is a misunderstanding.

423
00:40:45,813 --> 00:40:48,149
Just leave us alone!

424
00:40:48,816 --> 00:40:50,952
You can stay in there
if it makes you feel better.

425
00:40:51,018 --> 00:40:52,653
It does.

426
00:40:52,720 --> 00:40:54,422
Evelyn's in trouble.
Where is she?

427
00:40:54,487 --> 00:40:55,756
I don't know!

428
00:40:55,823 --> 00:40:57,758
And I wouldn't tell you
if I did.

429
00:40:57,825 --> 00:40:59,293
Is she still in the house?

430
00:40:59,360 --> 00:41:01,662
What the fuck did I just say?

431
00:41:01,729 --> 00:41:05,266
Nothing I can tell you will
make you believe me.

432
00:41:05,333 --> 00:41:08,536
Hell, I didn't believe it myself
and I lived through it.

433
00:41:08,536 --> 00:41:09,971
Through what?

434
00:41:11,238 --> 00:41:12,940
We had a child.

435
00:41:14,842 --> 00:41:17,545
She died because
we couldn't protect her.

436
00:41:19,013 --> 00:41:20,247
That's a lie.

437
00:41:20,314 --> 00:41:23,451
We could've protected her,
but we got careless.

438
00:41:24,251 --> 00:41:27,822
We thought we knew better
and it destroyed us.

439
00:41:27,888 --> 00:41:30,925
Evelyn never forgave herself
and...

440
00:41:30,992 --> 00:41:32,860
And what?

441
00:41:33,661 --> 00:41:35,629
She was my first love,
you know?

442
00:41:35,696 --> 00:41:37,398
Randall, we got her!

443
00:41:37,465 --> 00:41:39,000
Just leave her alone!

444
00:41:39,066 --> 00:41:42,203
I'm sorry.
This is for your own good.

445
00:41:44,705 --> 00:41:46,140
Let me out!

446
00:41:56,183 --> 00:42:00,287
Randall, Peter, we got her.

447
00:42:02,123 --> 00:42:03,190
Calm down.

448
00:42:03,257 --> 00:42:05,659
Get out of my house!

449
00:42:05,726 --> 00:42:07,728
Take a deep breath.
Calm down.

450
00:42:07,795 --> 00:42:08,829
Don't touch me.

451
00:42:08,896 --> 00:42:10,731
Everything is gonna be okay.

452
00:42:10,798 --> 00:42:13,734
Of course, it's you.
Stay away.

453
00:42:13,801 --> 00:42:17,204
Peter, give her some space.

454
00:42:19,607 --> 00:42:24,111
Evelyn, put that down.
You shouldn't be touching that.

455
00:42:25,613 --> 00:42:29,150
Please, hand it over, Evie.

456
00:42:31,419 --> 00:42:32,753
Let me take it off your hands.

457
00:42:32,820 --> 00:42:34,889
I just want to put it
someplace safe.

458
00:42:34,955 --> 00:42:38,092
There is no place safe.

459
00:42:38,159 --> 00:42:40,394
It was safe until you started
messing with it.

460
00:42:40,461 --> 00:42:41,629
Why, Evie?

461
00:42:41,662 --> 00:42:44,765
Because I miss her!

462
00:42:44,832 --> 00:42:46,634
I'm sorry about
the way things turned out.

463
00:42:46,667 --> 00:42:48,969
Yeah, you left me
right after she died

464
00:42:49,036 --> 00:42:51,238
when I needed you the most.

465
00:42:52,406 --> 00:42:54,475
What do you want me to say?

466
00:42:54,543 --> 00:42:56,644
That I couldn't face you after?

467
00:42:56,644 --> 00:42:59,680
That the-- the guilt
ate me up inside?

468
00:42:59,747 --> 00:43:02,950
I got it wrong and I've had
to live with that.

469
00:43:04,553 --> 00:43:05,820
But I can do it right this time.

470
00:43:05,886 --> 00:43:08,189
I know how. Trust me.

471
00:43:08,255 --> 00:43:09,890
Trust you?

472
00:43:09,957 --> 00:43:12,193
That's what got her killed.

473
00:43:12,960 --> 00:43:16,230
I translated one of the words
that you sent me.

474
00:43:17,566 --> 00:43:20,101
It's an incantation, isn't it?

475
00:43:20,167 --> 00:43:21,702
Tell me!

476
00:43:21,769 --> 00:43:23,671
We can still do the right thing.

477
00:43:24,472 --> 00:43:28,109
That's your weakness, always
wanting to do the right thing,

478
00:43:28,175 --> 00:43:32,913
huh, when there's only pain
and loss and suffering.

479
00:43:32,980 --> 00:43:36,117
This is not going
to bring Sarah back!

480
00:43:37,284 --> 00:43:38,686
Give it to me!

481
00:43:39,253 --> 00:43:44,892
Why?
So you can bury me again?

482
00:43:44,959 --> 00:43:47,928
Who-- who am I talking
to right now?

483
00:43:47,995 --> 00:43:50,698
What have you done with Evelyn?

484
00:43:50,764 --> 00:43:53,602
I wear her like a coat.

485
00:44:08,583 --> 00:44:09,750
Oh, my God.

486
00:44:09,817 --> 00:44:10,818
Let's get outta here.

487
00:44:10,885 --> 00:44:12,820
Oh, let's call the others.

488
00:44:12,887 --> 00:44:15,089
Get out, quick, quick.

489
00:46:08,637 --> 00:46:12,540
Evelyn? Evelyn?

490
00:46:16,910 --> 00:46:19,413
Oh, my God,
what did they do to you?

491
00:46:20,414 --> 00:46:21,849
They're gone now.

492
00:46:22,550 --> 00:46:26,153
Let's get you changed.
Oh, my goodness.

493
00:46:26,220 --> 00:46:29,957
Here we go.
Where are you hurt?

494
00:46:31,526 --> 00:46:34,395
Oh, look at your hand.
What did they do to you?

495
00:46:34,461 --> 00:46:38,866
Okay, let's-- let's sit here.
Yeah, there you go.

496
00:46:40,868 --> 00:46:42,069
-Want to give me that?
-No.

497
00:46:42,136 --> 00:46:43,971
Wash your hands, okay?

498
00:46:44,038 --> 00:46:45,973
Okay. Okay. Here we go.

499
00:46:47,875 --> 00:46:52,112
All right. There you go.

500
00:46:53,280 --> 00:46:55,482
Got this one.
That's great.

501
00:46:58,886 --> 00:47:00,588
Where's your phone?

502
00:47:00,655 --> 00:47:02,956
-In the office.
-Okay.

503
00:47:04,091 --> 00:47:08,195
We'll find it, yeah?
You'll be okay.

504
00:47:08,262 --> 00:47:09,897
Yeah.

505
00:47:11,800 --> 00:47:13,467
Here we are. All right.

506
00:47:14,769 --> 00:47:16,904
Okay, you good?

507
00:47:16,937 --> 00:47:20,974
-Yeah, I'm fine.
-All right. Here we are.

508
00:47:25,814 --> 00:47:29,684
All right.
Let's sit right here.

509
00:47:29,751 --> 00:47:31,485
Where is it?

510
00:47:32,620 --> 00:47:35,657
Okay, great.

511
00:47:35,724 --> 00:47:37,559
For fuck's sake!

512
00:47:38,992 --> 00:47:40,994
What do they want?

513
00:47:42,463 --> 00:47:45,032
What-- this?
What-- what is it?

514
00:47:45,099 --> 00:47:47,334
Is it worth a lot of money?

515
00:47:52,707 --> 00:47:54,241
This is not--

516
00:47:56,443 --> 00:47:58,946
You should be surrounded
by loved ones,

517
00:47:59,012 --> 00:48:01,115
not by someone like me.

518
00:48:04,084 --> 00:48:07,121
<i>Sarah, if you ever get</i>
<i>to hear this,</i>

519
00:48:07,187 --> 00:48:10,692
<i>your suffering is</i>
<i>because of us.</i>

520
00:48:10,759 --> 00:48:13,460
<i>Too many risks.</i>

521
00:48:13,528 --> 00:48:16,163
<i>Too much contact</i>
<i>with the other side.</i>

522
00:48:16,230 --> 00:48:18,132
<i>We have to bury her.</i>

523
00:48:18,198 --> 00:48:20,968
<i>I'm sorry we put</i>
<i>all this ahead of you.</i>

524
00:48:21,034 --> 00:48:23,638
<i>I'll never expose you</i>
<i>to this again.</i>

525
00:48:24,672 --> 00:48:26,140
<i>What's wrong with us?</i>

526
00:48:26,206 --> 00:48:28,976
<i>Okay. Father, start the prayer.</i>

527
00:48:30,879 --> 00:48:32,980
<i>I'm sorry.</i>
<i>It was meant for--</i>

528
00:48:33,046 --> 00:48:34,582
<i>Stop, stop.</i>
<i>Please don't do this.</i>

529
00:48:34,649 --> 00:48:36,851
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

530
00:48:36,984 --> 00:48:38,185
Is that...

531
00:48:38,252 --> 00:48:39,554
<i>Help me. Mommy!</i>

532
00:48:39,621 --> 00:48:41,155
-...your baby?
<i>-No, mommy, please.</i>

533
00:48:41,221 --> 00:48:42,624
<i>She's not okay.</i>

534
00:48:42,690 --> 00:48:44,158
<i>She will be fine.</i>

535
00:48:44,224 --> 00:48:45,560
<i>Stop! Stop!</i>

536
00:48:45,627 --> 00:48:47,227
<i>She'll look in the box.</i>

537
00:48:47,294 --> 00:48:48,228
<i>What-- what is this?</i>

538
00:48:51,465 --> 00:48:52,834
<i>Look at her!</i>

539
00:48:52,901 --> 00:48:54,201
<i>Help!</i>

540
00:48:55,804 --> 00:48:57,438
<i>Stop! Stop! Stop!</i>

541
00:48:57,505 --> 00:48:59,106
<i>There he is.</i>

542
00:48:59,173 --> 00:49:00,708
<i>Get off!</i>

543
00:49:00,775 --> 00:49:02,777
<i>We've got to bury the de--</i>

544
00:49:03,243 --> 00:49:05,245
Let's get you warmed up.

545
00:49:13,888 --> 00:49:16,658
I brought her to evil.

546
00:49:16,724 --> 00:49:19,092
It's my fault.

547
00:49:19,159 --> 00:49:21,696
-It's all my fault.
-Don't say that.

548
00:49:24,498 --> 00:49:26,033
It's true.

549
00:49:26,099 --> 00:49:29,637
All right. You're okay.

550
00:49:29,704 --> 00:49:31,038
Okay.

551
00:49:31,104 --> 00:49:33,575
No, no. I don't want it.

552
00:49:33,641 --> 00:49:35,209
Okay.

553
00:49:42,216 --> 00:49:45,720
Nice, nice, nice, nice, nice.
You feeling better?

554
00:49:48,222 --> 00:49:49,189
This one's nice.

555
00:49:55,930 --> 00:49:57,464
Things happen, Evelyn.

556
00:49:57,532 --> 00:50:00,234
I'm sure you and Randall
were great parents.

557
00:50:01,936 --> 00:50:04,137
You don't know that.

558
00:50:06,139 --> 00:50:09,142
I know I blamed myself
for my mom's death.

559
00:50:10,745 --> 00:50:15,382
I mean, I know,
I didn't make her sick,

560
00:50:15,449 --> 00:50:19,787
but I-- I should've been there
for her, and I-- I just-- I--

561
00:50:19,854 --> 00:50:21,355
I couldn't do it.

562
00:50:23,190 --> 00:50:25,994
It's easier to take care
of strangers.

563
00:50:26,059 --> 00:50:27,127
Hmm.

564
00:50:30,063 --> 00:50:33,601
Fuck's sake.
Just stay here.

565
00:50:34,669 --> 00:50:36,604
I just want to talk!

566
00:50:38,006 --> 00:50:40,474
Please just don't move!

567
00:50:45,078 --> 00:50:46,313
I called the cops!

568
00:50:46,380 --> 00:50:48,215
You need to get
the fuck outta here now!

569
00:50:48,282 --> 00:50:49,751
Listen to me.

570
00:50:50,585 --> 00:50:54,121
I know it's confusing, but--
but that's not Evelyn in there.

571
00:50:54,187 --> 00:50:55,890
It's something dangerous.

572
00:50:55,957 --> 00:50:58,458
The only dangerous thing here
is you and your psycho friends!

573
00:50:58,526 --> 00:51:01,428
She killed Peter!
He's dead because of her!

574
00:51:01,495 --> 00:51:04,632
She didn't kill anybody!
She's fucking old!

575
00:51:05,800 --> 00:51:07,535
Stay the fuck back!

576
00:51:09,403 --> 00:51:11,739
That little ivory statue
that she has,

577
00:51:11,806 --> 00:51:14,742
you're not safe as long
as that thing is in the house.

578
00:51:14,809 --> 00:51:16,578
The statue is the problem?

579
00:51:16,644 --> 00:51:19,479
It's an anchor, a vessel
for something dark.

580
00:51:19,547 --> 00:51:21,148
It's attached itself to her.

581
00:51:21,214 --> 00:51:22,850
What the fuck
are you talking about?

582
00:51:22,917 --> 00:51:26,153
It'll kill you both!
We can't leave here without--

583
00:51:26,219 --> 00:51:27,522
Okay, fine!

584
00:51:27,589 --> 00:51:29,289
If I get it for you,
will you leave?

585
00:51:29,356 --> 00:51:31,358
Yes.
That's all we want!

586
00:51:31,425 --> 00:51:33,728
Just stay outside.
I'll go get it!

587
00:51:34,261 --> 00:51:36,263
You're doing the right thing.

588
00:51:42,336 --> 00:51:44,973
You think you can
take this from me?

589
00:51:45,039 --> 00:51:46,273
Huh?

590
00:51:47,008 --> 00:51:50,377
For fuck's sake, Evelyn,
I told you to stay over there!

591
00:51:50,444 --> 00:51:51,679
Put the knife down!

592
00:51:51,746 --> 00:51:54,181
No!

593
00:51:54,181 --> 00:51:55,449
Please, let's talk.

594
00:51:55,516 --> 00:51:58,418
Maybe we can work
something out with them.

595
00:51:58,485 --> 00:52:00,788
Evelyn, everything's
gonna be okay.

596
00:52:00,855 --> 00:52:02,189
You're safe.
Why don't you just give me--

597
00:52:02,255 --> 00:52:05,593
No! No!

598
00:52:06,794 --> 00:52:08,796
Evelyn, stop!

599
00:52:08,863 --> 00:52:10,798
You, stop!

600
00:52:10,865 --> 00:52:12,867
Evelyn, stop.

601
00:52:16,904 --> 00:52:18,405
Where are you?

602
00:52:23,911 --> 00:52:25,780
Fuck.

603
00:52:37,892 --> 00:52:39,426
Evelyn?

604
00:52:51,238 --> 00:52:52,807
Hello?

605
00:54:25,233 --> 00:54:26,934
Hurry up!

606
00:54:28,236 --> 00:54:29,170
Come on.

607
00:54:29,237 --> 00:54:30,805
You're here.

608
00:54:32,907 --> 00:54:36,043
We can still salvage this.
Trust me.

609
00:54:36,110 --> 00:54:37,712
Like Peter did?

610
00:54:39,346 --> 00:54:40,515
What is this?

611
00:54:40,581 --> 00:54:42,049
What are we dealing
with, Randall?

612
00:54:42,116 --> 00:54:44,018
Nothing I can't handle.

613
00:54:52,459 --> 00:54:53,761
What happened?

614
00:54:53,828 --> 00:54:57,131
We were too late.
It's already in her.

615
00:54:58,032 --> 00:55:00,935
We lost Peter,
there was nothing we could do.

616
00:55:02,369 --> 00:55:04,404
We need to get it
into the statue

617
00:55:04,471 --> 00:55:06,473
and back in here.

618
00:55:09,644 --> 00:55:13,281
Randall, this is very dangerous.

619
00:55:13,380 --> 00:55:14,882
It's not because
I'm no longer authorized.

620
00:55:14,949 --> 00:55:16,184
It's--

621
00:55:16,250 --> 00:55:19,020
You remember what happened
last time we tried this?

622
00:55:19,086 --> 00:55:21,388
You're all I've got.

623
00:55:21,454 --> 00:55:23,858
I'm not gonna lose
both of them.

624
00:55:25,126 --> 00:55:26,426
I understand.

625
00:55:26,493 --> 00:55:30,397
Randall, this one,
this one is strong.

626
00:55:30,397 --> 00:55:33,868
Stronger than anything
we ever faced before
and you know it.

627
00:55:34,401 --> 00:55:36,704
-This time is different.
-What's this?

628
00:55:36,771 --> 00:55:40,641
We can destroy it.
We only need one word.

629
00:55:40,708 --> 00:55:44,579
This is an incantation
of the blood of Christ.

630
00:55:45,680 --> 00:55:49,016
Blood of Christ.
Evelyn figured it out.

631
00:55:50,084 --> 00:55:51,953
No more hiding it away.

632
00:55:52,019 --> 00:55:55,523
I can finally make it pay
for everything that it's done.

633
00:55:55,590 --> 00:55:57,792
Send it back to hell
where it belongs.

634
00:55:57,859 --> 00:56:02,763
Hey, if this time
it doesn't work?

635
00:56:02,830 --> 00:56:05,633
We're going through the front.

636
00:56:05,700 --> 00:56:08,636
Stick together, near the back.

637
00:56:08,703 --> 00:56:12,540
Holler if you see her.

638
00:56:12,607 --> 00:56:16,644
Don't do anything
until I'm there.

639
00:56:18,012 --> 00:56:19,614
Go on.

640
00:56:21,616 --> 00:56:23,483
I'm going to fix this.

641
00:56:35,229 --> 00:56:37,531
She's stronger than she looks.

642
00:56:38,933 --> 00:56:42,469
If it goes south,
just run out.

643
00:56:49,277 --> 00:56:52,647
Evelyn, is that you?

644
00:57:01,689 --> 00:57:05,326
<i>Honey, do you know</i>
<i>why you're here?</i>

645
00:57:06,594 --> 00:57:09,697
<i>Why-- why are my hands tied?</i>
- What the hell?

646
00:57:09,764 --> 00:57:13,234
<i>So you don't</i>
<i>hurt yourself again.</i>

647
00:57:13,301 --> 00:57:15,236
<i>Remember last night?</i>

648
00:57:15,303 --> 00:57:17,238
<i>No.</i>

649
00:57:17,305 --> 00:57:19,707
<i>You scratched</i>
<i>until your face bled.</i>

650
00:57:19,774 --> 00:57:22,109
<i>Stop it.</i>

651
00:57:23,811 --> 00:57:25,246
<i>How do you feel?</i>

652
00:57:25,313 --> 00:57:27,581
<i>My tummy really hurts.</i>

653
00:57:30,785 --> 00:57:33,521
<i>I don't feel good.</i>

654
00:57:33,521 --> 00:57:36,190
<i>Do you remember</i>
<i>when we went on the dig?</i>

655
00:57:39,126 --> 00:57:41,028
<i>Do you remember</i>
<i>what school you go to?</i>

656
00:57:41,095 --> 00:57:44,031
<i>No! No!</i>

657
00:57:44,098 --> 00:57:46,367
<i>What do you remember?</i>

658
00:57:46,434 --> 00:57:47,868
<i>No. Mommy!</i>

659
00:57:47,935 --> 00:57:50,004
<i>Sarah?</i>

660
00:57:50,071 --> 00:57:52,073
<i>I pray the soul</i>
<i>is another body to take.</i>

661
00:57:52,139 --> 00:57:54,408
<i>I only remember</i>
<i>that you're a shit mother!</i>

662
00:57:54,542 --> 00:57:55,910
<i>Sarah!</i>

663
00:57:55,977 --> 00:57:57,144
<i>Randall!</i>

664
00:57:58,612 --> 00:58:00,314
<i>Oh, my God.</i>

665
00:58:00,381 --> 00:58:01,916
<i>Is that all you've got,</i>
<i>old man?</i>

666
00:58:01,983 --> 00:58:03,551
<i>Hmm?</i>

667
00:58:03,551 --> 00:58:04,952
<i>Stop it!</i>

668
00:58:05,019 --> 00:58:06,554
<i>No!</i>

669
00:58:06,587 --> 00:58:07,722
<i>Look at her!</i>

670
00:58:07,788 --> 00:58:09,190
<i>No!</i>

671
00:58:09,256 --> 00:58:10,391
<i>What have we done?</i>

672
00:58:14,962 --> 00:58:16,764
Shit.

673
00:58:56,971 --> 00:58:59,407
Evelyn, where have you been?

674
00:58:59,473 --> 00:59:01,609
Why do you have that?

675
00:59:02,877 --> 00:59:04,879
You're scaring me.

676
00:59:06,213 --> 00:59:08,215
Please don't hurt me.

677
00:59:10,618 --> 00:59:12,987
Why are you following me?

678
00:59:13,954 --> 00:59:18,292
I was looking for you.
Where were you?

679
00:59:19,326 --> 00:59:21,530
Do you remember anything?

680
00:59:21,629 --> 00:59:24,932
I remember some things.

681
00:59:26,100 --> 00:59:28,903
I had a dream about my mother,

682
00:59:29,904 --> 00:59:33,040
not long after she passed.

683
00:59:33,107 --> 00:59:36,944
We were making dinner together,
like every other night.

684
00:59:37,011 --> 00:59:39,847
And right in the middle,
she stopped

685
00:59:39,914 --> 00:59:41,682
and said she had to go.

686
00:59:41,749 --> 00:59:46,720
So I ran after her
to say goodbye,

687
00:59:47,955 --> 00:59:52,059
but she kept walking
like she didn't hear me.

688
00:59:52,126 --> 00:59:55,863
So I followed her,
but she was lost,

689
00:59:55,930 --> 01:00:00,067
disappeared into the fog.

690
01:00:03,037 --> 01:00:07,842
How do you know that?
I never told you that.

691
01:00:49,183 --> 01:00:51,986
I never told you that.

692
01:00:54,221 --> 01:00:58,826
Evelyn?
Stop, you're freaking me out.

693
01:01:06,800 --> 01:01:12,773
Jules? Jules.

694
01:01:18,045 --> 01:01:19,813
Mom?

695
01:01:27,121 --> 01:01:30,157
Can you come here, please?

696
01:01:33,562 --> 01:01:35,863
I missed you, <i>mija.</i>

697
01:01:35,930 --> 01:01:37,765
This can't...

698
01:01:37,765 --> 01:01:39,867
The last time I saw you
was at the airport.

699
01:01:39,934 --> 01:01:44,573
We were saying goodbye
and the sunlight
was shining behind you.

700
01:01:44,639 --> 01:01:46,974
- And it was so beautiful.
- You're not my mom.

701
01:01:47,041 --> 01:01:48,943
Oh, Jules,

702
01:01:49,009 --> 01:01:53,480
remember when you were five
and broke your arm?

703
01:01:53,548 --> 01:01:57,351
-Who fed you every meal?
-No. Stop it. Stop it.
Please, stop.

704
01:01:57,418 --> 01:01:59,554
When you were 12 and missed
a month of school

705
01:01:59,621 --> 01:02:03,791
with pneumonia,
who nursed you back to health?

706
01:02:03,824 --> 01:02:05,926
Who cried with you
when your prom date

707
01:02:05,993 --> 01:02:07,795
didn't show up?

708
01:02:07,795 --> 01:02:11,232
-I held you. I comforted you.
-Stop.

709
01:02:11,298 --> 01:02:13,635
I was there for you.
<i>- No puedo...</i>

710
01:02:13,702 --> 01:02:16,503
It's so cold here.
- Stop it.

711
01:02:16,571 --> 01:02:19,340
Please.
Let me see you again.

712
01:02:19,406 --> 01:02:21,809
I said stop it!

713
01:02:24,378 --> 01:02:26,514
<i>Te quiero, mija.</i>

714
01:03:00,381 --> 01:03:01,382
Okay.

715
01:03:01,448 --> 01:03:03,417
Okay.

716
01:03:14,428 --> 01:03:16,964
Oh, okay.

717
01:03:27,441 --> 01:03:28,876
Okay.

718
01:03:37,184 --> 01:03:38,553
Okay.

719
01:03:46,695 --> 01:03:50,998
Oh, what is this?

720
01:04:07,114 --> 01:04:08,916
What is this?

721
01:04:46,453 --> 01:04:48,188
Evelyn!

722
01:04:48,255 --> 01:04:50,190
Way too late.
Time's over.

723
01:04:50,257 --> 01:04:52,159
Edgar, hold her!

724
01:04:53,561 --> 01:04:54,696
Please, hear us!

725
01:04:54,763 --> 01:04:56,497
Nobody's listening!

726
01:05:03,538 --> 01:05:05,272
Surrender her! Don't listen.

727
01:05:05,339 --> 01:05:07,776
By the power of God,
surrender her.

728
01:05:07,842 --> 01:05:10,812
You don't stand a chance!

729
01:05:16,250 --> 01:05:19,821
Oh, shit. Fuck!
I don't have my keys.

730
01:05:19,888 --> 01:05:21,288
I don't have my keys.

731
01:05:23,357 --> 01:05:24,491
Oh, huh, wait!

732
01:05:26,160 --> 01:05:28,696
Just get your fucking keys
and get outta here.

733
01:05:31,766 --> 01:05:36,638
Oh, God, thrust into Hell
Satan and all evil spirits

734
01:05:36,704 --> 01:05:40,909
who wander through the world
for the ruin of souls.

735
01:05:41,008 --> 01:05:42,042
Amen.

736
01:05:42,109 --> 01:05:43,511
Stupid priest.

737
01:05:43,578 --> 01:05:46,113
Evelyn, stop.
Be careful!

738
01:05:46,180 --> 01:05:47,481
Get outta here!

739
01:05:47,549 --> 01:05:50,017
Evelyn, fight it.
I know you can.

740
01:05:50,017 --> 01:05:54,021
In the name of God, the Father,
Jesus Christ the Son,

741
01:05:54,087 --> 01:05:56,925
and by the power
of the Holy Spirit,

742
01:05:57,024 --> 01:05:59,259
you will obey me,
you foul thing.

743
01:05:59,326 --> 01:06:03,631
God cast you into a pit
of hellfire, into that pit
you shall return.

744
01:06:03,698 --> 01:06:07,334
Oh, I can already
feel her suffering.

745
01:06:07,401 --> 01:06:09,470
Evelyn is stronger
than you will ever be.

746
01:06:09,537 --> 01:06:11,873
That's not
who I'm talking about.

747
01:06:11,940 --> 01:06:15,275
Your daughter
is in eternal torture,
because of you.

748
01:06:15,342 --> 01:06:19,848
You failed her, but I,
I can bring her peace.

749
01:06:21,281 --> 01:06:22,784
Don't listen to it.

750
01:06:22,851 --> 01:06:24,552
Leave the flesh
of God's righteous creature

751
01:06:24,619 --> 01:06:28,590
and return to the darkness
from whence you came!

752
01:06:28,656 --> 01:06:33,427
Ah, your souls or hers!

753
01:06:33,494 --> 01:06:38,867
-Little Sarah's blossoming
into a lovely woman.
-Shut your mouth, demon!

754
01:06:38,933 --> 01:06:42,069
Oh, you should be honored
to have made

755
01:06:42,135 --> 01:06:44,271
such a precious sacrifice
for me.

756
01:06:44,338 --> 01:06:47,174
I have them both now,
and Evelyn has given up

757
01:06:47,241 --> 01:06:50,177
her defiance
and replaced it with screams.

758
01:06:50,244 --> 01:06:52,079
It's a sweet symphony!

759
01:06:52,145 --> 01:06:53,180
Evie, fight it.

760
01:06:53,247 --> 01:06:55,215
You're stronger than this thing.

761
01:06:55,282 --> 01:06:57,685
You told me that you
found a way and you did.

762
01:06:57,752 --> 01:07:00,187
But I need your help,
so fight it.

763
01:07:00,254 --> 01:07:02,790
Fight it for her!
Fight it for all of us!

764
01:07:04,626 --> 01:07:07,494
The blood of Christ
seals the cage.

765
01:07:07,562 --> 01:07:11,533
By all that's holy in the power
of the Kingdom of Heaven,

766
01:07:11,599 --> 01:07:16,004
I banish you!
Return to your prison.

767
01:07:17,672 --> 01:07:19,574
Your soul's it is.

768
01:07:56,611 --> 01:07:58,680
Make it stop.

769
01:09:57,565 --> 01:09:59,867
What have you done, Evelyn?

770
01:10:10,645 --> 01:10:12,580
You can't leave.

771
01:10:12,647 --> 01:10:14,515
We need to get you
to a hospital.

772
01:10:14,582 --> 01:10:16,017
Come on, let's get you
to my car.

773
01:10:16,084 --> 01:10:17,350
I can't.

774
01:10:17,417 --> 01:10:20,888
Just try
or you'll bleed to death.

775
01:10:20,955 --> 01:10:22,489
Please, help me save her.

776
01:10:22,557 --> 01:10:24,892
What is wrong with you people?

777
01:10:24,959 --> 01:10:26,728
When this is over, bury it.

778
01:10:26,794 --> 01:10:27,962
What?

779
01:10:28,029 --> 01:10:31,599
When everything is done,
put it in the ground.

780
01:10:31,666 --> 01:10:33,735
It's just like in the basement.

781
01:10:33,801 --> 01:10:35,670
Like, what these?

782
01:10:36,871 --> 01:10:37,872
Yeah.

783
01:10:37,939 --> 01:10:39,073
And then-- and then--
and then,

784
01:10:39,140 --> 01:10:40,708
there were these letters.

785
01:10:40,775 --> 01:10:43,711
E-L-I-M.

786
01:10:44,779 --> 01:10:46,013
Elim.

787
01:10:47,014 --> 01:10:49,150
What does it mean?

788
01:10:49,217 --> 01:10:50,752
We need to hurry.

789
01:10:52,419 --> 01:10:54,055
No. No, please, let me go.

790
01:10:54,122 --> 01:10:55,923
You can't go.

791
01:10:55,990 --> 01:10:58,226
My dad needs me.

792
01:10:58,291 --> 01:11:01,495
Don't let Evelyn die alone.

793
01:11:03,396 --> 01:11:04,832
Come with me.

794
01:11:04,899 --> 01:11:08,936
Listen, a Christian
ritual's satanic,

795
01:11:09,003 --> 01:11:11,873
but if Elim seals the cage,

796
01:11:11,939 --> 01:11:15,176
Satanism names our power.

797
01:11:15,243 --> 01:11:17,945
I can kill this thing.

798
01:11:18,012 --> 01:11:19,714
I don't wanna do it.

799
01:11:34,028 --> 01:11:36,363
No, I don't wanna--
I don't wanna do it.

800
01:11:38,365 --> 01:11:41,102
It should be a perfect fit.

801
01:11:41,169 --> 01:11:44,071
Where do we-- wait.

802
01:11:44,138 --> 01:11:46,874
Where are you--

803
01:11:46,941 --> 01:11:47,975
Where are you going?

804
01:11:51,378 --> 01:11:52,914
Just let me leave.

805
01:11:52,980 --> 01:11:53,915
Please.

806
01:11:59,452 --> 01:12:00,855
No!

807
01:12:17,772 --> 01:12:22,076
Julia? Oh, Julia?

808
01:12:24,846 --> 01:12:29,250
Don't be afraid, darling Julia.

809
01:12:29,317 --> 01:12:33,420
Your mother wasn't.

810
01:12:33,453 --> 01:12:37,959
She wasn't afraid to die.
She was heartbroken.

811
01:12:39,327 --> 01:12:42,630
And I know her pain.

812
01:12:47,001 --> 01:12:49,436
You don't know my mother.

813
01:12:49,502 --> 01:12:52,173
I know her suffering.

814
01:12:52,240 --> 01:12:55,643
And soon you'll have yours!

815
01:12:55,710 --> 01:12:57,444
Go away!

816
01:13:29,343 --> 01:13:30,477
Okay.

817
01:13:30,544 --> 01:13:31,979
We're doing...

818
01:13:47,995 --> 01:13:49,563
Where did it go?

819
01:13:49,630 --> 01:13:52,199
Where does it fucking fit?

820
01:13:57,805 --> 01:14:00,007
What am I supposed to do?

821
01:14:08,182 --> 01:14:13,220
Oh, no, we won't be
needing that anymore.

822
01:14:18,392 --> 01:14:19,927
Tell me, Julia,

823
01:14:19,994 --> 01:14:23,864
would you trade your soul
for hers?

824
01:14:23,931 --> 01:14:25,833
I'm not cutting
any deals with you!

825
01:14:25,900 --> 01:14:29,036
You've abandoned her
like your mother.

826
01:14:34,942 --> 01:14:40,881
The human body is much more fun
than a little statue.

827
01:14:40,948 --> 01:14:43,384
And this one is very tired.

828
01:14:43,451 --> 01:14:44,585
Let her go!

829
01:14:44,652 --> 01:14:46,387
I intend to.

830
01:14:47,455 --> 01:14:49,256
What do you want?

831
01:14:49,323 --> 01:14:52,626
Right now, you!

832
01:15:13,481 --> 01:15:17,084
Sarah doesn't blame you.

833
01:15:20,488 --> 01:15:24,191
It was never your fault.

834
01:15:58,192 --> 01:16:01,629
We did it. We did it.

835
01:16:03,330 --> 01:16:05,099
I'm free.

836
01:16:14,308 --> 01:16:18,245
I think I need a hospital.

837
01:16:21,749 --> 01:16:25,453
Wait, I don't, I don't feel...

838
01:16:31,526 --> 01:16:33,294
What's happening?

839
01:16:33,360 --> 01:16:37,665
I'm sorry.
It has to be this way.

840
01:16:38,866 --> 01:16:40,935
What are you doing?

841
01:16:44,872 --> 01:16:48,876
The only way is if it dies
inside a living vessel.

842
01:16:53,080 --> 01:16:55,349
I have to do it now
while it's weak.

843
01:16:56,450 --> 01:16:58,686
Or before I forget.

844
01:17:00,855 --> 01:17:01,989
Please.

845
01:17:04,258 --> 01:17:09,897
You have been the answer
to all my prayers.

846
01:17:15,604 --> 01:17:16,605
No!

847
01:17:20,007 --> 01:17:23,310
Please, don't kill me!

848
01:17:23,377 --> 01:17:25,212
Not again!

849
01:17:34,221 --> 01:17:35,557
No!

850
01:17:35,624 --> 01:17:37,424
Please, stop!

851
01:17:42,930 --> 01:17:45,199
Please, don't!

852
01:17:46,734 --> 01:17:48,570
Please, don't kill me!

853
01:17:48,637 --> 01:17:50,539
Help me!

854
01:17:52,907 --> 01:17:55,409
Mommy!

855
01:17:56,310 --> 01:17:59,313
Help! Please, help!

856
01:17:59,847 --> 01:18:02,116
Help! Please, help!

857
01:18:03,017 --> 01:18:05,419
Mommy, please help!

858
01:18:05,486 --> 01:18:09,223
Evelyn, what are you doing?

859
01:18:11,626 --> 01:18:12,893
Help, help!

860
01:18:12,960 --> 01:18:17,398
You cannot bury me again.

861
01:18:24,371 --> 01:18:25,674
Evelyn!

862
01:18:25,773 --> 01:18:27,408
Don't!

863
01:18:47,461 --> 01:18:52,967
<i>♪ Take the name of Jesus</i>
<i>with you ♪</i>

864
01:18:53,033 --> 01:18:58,506
<i>♪ Child of sorrow and of woe ♪</i>

865
01:18:58,573 --> 01:19:04,245
<i>♪ It will joy</i>
<i>and comfort give you ♪</i>

866
01:19:04,311 --> 01:19:09,316
<i>♪ Take it then</i>
<i>wherever you go ♪</i>

867
01:19:09,383 --> 01:19:11,720
<i>-♪ Precious name ♪</i>
<i>-♪ Precious name ♪</i>

868
01:19:11,819 --> 01:19:14,723
<i>-♪ Oh, how sweet ♪</i>
<i>-♪ Oh, how sweet ♪</i>

869
01:19:14,822 --> 01:19:18,560
<i>♪ Hope of Earth</i>
<i>and joy of Heav'n... ♪</i>
